  data: {
    LLM: 'Four cards dealt to each player. Players declare in or out simultaneously (e.g. coin in closed fist; those with a coin are in). Dealer deals three common cards face up. Each player in forms best five-card hand from four hole cards plus three board cards (seven cards total). Best hand wins pot; all others who stayed in match the pot. If only one stays in, that player wins the pot without showing. Game ends when one player wins the whole pot by being the only one in.',
    Player: 'Four cards dealt to each player. Players declare in or out simultaneously (e.g. coin in closed fist; those with a coin are in). Dealer deals three common cards face up. Each player in forms best five-card hand from four hole cards plus three board cards (seven cards total). Best hand wins pot; all others who stayed in match the pot. If only one stays in, that player wins the pot without showing. Game ends when one player wins the whole pot by being the only one in.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the best five-card poker hand among those who stayed in, or win without contest if you are the only player in.',
    gameplay: 'Four cards dealt to each player. Players declare in or out simultaneously (e.g. coin in closed fist; those with a coin are in). Dealer deals three common cards face up. Each player in forms best five-card hand from four hole cards plus three board cards (seven cards total). Best hand wins pot; all others who stayed in match the pot. If only one stays in, that player wins the pot without showing. Game ends when one player wins the whole pot by being the only one in.',
    keyRules: [
      'Four cards each, then simultaneous declare in or out',
